This application uses Ray Optics Simulation as a conceptual and algorithmic reference for a 2D geometric-optics simulator. The implementation in ПРЕЛОМ is an independent TypeScript rewrite and does not embed the upstream website, reuse its interface, or redistribute its graphical assets.

Adapted or reimplemented components:
- iterative ray propagation with bounded branching and bounce limits;
- geometric intersections between rays and line, circular and polygonal optical boundaries;
- reflection, Snell refraction and total internal reflection;
- wavelength-dependent refractive index for visible-light dispersion;
- partial reflection/transmission and intensity cutoffs;
- scene serialization concepts for editable optical objects.

Materially changed in ПРЕЛОМ:
- mobile-first product structure and gestures;
- object model and scene schema;
- rendering, visual modes, measurements and heat maps;
- adaptive quality and time-budget controls;
- preset experiments, task evaluation and local persistence;
- all user interface, styling, iconography and copy.

